{
  "_about": [
    "What a business owner should never read: one rule set for the chat (plainText.ts) and the expert style eval (backend copilot/eval/style/plain_language.py), so the two cannot drift.",
    "{NAME} is a word list matched in any case; {NAME:noabbr} the same, except an all-caps word of three letters or fewer, which reads as an abbreviation ('CD sales'); {NAME:exact} as written. {FRAGMENT} is pasted in first.",
    "'certain' rules fail the eval and hide a chat label. 'possible' rules hide a chat label but the eval only reports them: they also match prose ('a big bash', 'Running cat brief').",
    "A rule's term is its first capture group that matched, else the whole match. No lookbehind: older Safari cannot compile it.",
    "Every example must hold for both implementations; both test suites run them."
  ],
